message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on a pirate costume for adults. Costumes of festive character fall under heading 9505 only if not wearing apparel of textile... but note 11 to chapter 61 and 62 exclude carnival costumes? Actually, Chapter 95 note 1(e) excludes sports clothing; the heading 9505 covers festive articles. Textile costumes are classified in 9505 only if they're not "garments of ordinary apparel" — CBP typically classifies adult costumes made of textile in Chapter 61/62 if they're of apparel type, though costumes of festive nature fall in 9505.90.6000 ("Festive, carnival or other entertainment articles: Other: Other"). Wearing apparel of a festive nature was classified in 9505 per the Explanatory Notes, as long as the articles are not ordinary apparel. Since this is a set of dress, foam corset and hat, with the foam corset, it is likely classified in 9505.90.6000 as a festive article.

Note that the costume is for adults, and CBP rulings on adult costumes of this kind often state "The applicable subheading for the Playful Pirate costume will be 9505.90.6000, HTSUS, which provides for festive, carnival or other entertainment articles... other." This fits.

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "The adult pirate costume set (pullover dress, foam corset and hat) is a festive article of a type used for costume or entertainment, classified in heading 9505 as other festive, carnival or entertainment articles."}
